{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 125 backward-free multi-seed arms (`exp26`–`exp51`, plus 7 pullback and 15 exact-BP arms; $147$ arms $=440$ runs) on repeatedly inspected `DEV`/`VAL-B` splits over short horizons on ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route lexical credit via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), and prove the 4th-moment variance drop of reward tangent projection in the pre-rotary basis (Prop. 5). Fused Triton cuts `d6` WM time $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). On 360st `d6`, 4-mat WM hits $2.0682\\pm0.0006$ `DEV` BPB (vs. $2.0532$ 4-mat BP, $2.2603$ `SR-LNP`, $2.2415$ `SR-NP`); 6-mat $(W_Q,W_K)$ (`99.9978%` active) hits $2.0595\\pm0.0007$ ($M=2$, `9.35s`) and $2.0552\\pm0.0007$ ($M=4$, $60.2\\%$ of BP gain `2.0532->2.0316`), and at $720$st hits $1.9763\\pm0.0009$ ($M=2$, `21.67s`) and $1.9683\\pm0.0007$ ($M=4+$`ve_gate`, $59.0\\%$ of BP gain `1.9423->1.8904`). Full-depth 6-mat $M=2$ is unfavorable at equal time vs. extra-step 4-mat WM ($2.0454$ at $438$st; $1.9720$ at $1,004$st, `21.55s`), whereas Upper-Half `(3,4,5)` probing captures $92.9\\%$ of the 720st gain (`1.9779`, `18.59s`) and **beats 1,004st 4-mat WM at matched `~21.6s` time ($840$st: $1.9609\\pm0.0006$ `DEV`, $1.9264\\pm0.0007$ `VAL-B`, $218.03$ PPL)**. On 100st `50.3M`, isolated Triton speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$ ($M_g=1$), hitting $1.8978\\pm0.0007$ (4-mat) and **$1.8853\\pm0.0013$ `DEV` BPB ($201.21$ PPL, $10.24$ GiB) on 6-mat $M=2$ ($99.9990\\%$ active)**, trailing 6-mat BP ($1.8904$ on 720st `d6`; $1.6989$ on `50.3M`).",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Executed 13 new 3-seed arms on ClimbMix d6 (39 new runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48 in exp50_d6_equal_compute_qk_schedules_results.json and exp51_d6_720step_scaling_and_bp_controls_results.json; total 147 multi-seed arms = 440 runs): (a) Selective Layerwise (W_Q, W_K) Probing: At 720 steps, Upper-Half blocks (3,4,5) M=2 reaches 1.9779 +- 0.0006 DEV BPB (1.9431 +- 0.0007 VAL-B, 228.40 PPL in 18.59s), capturing 92.9% of the full 6-block M=2 gain (1.9763 vs. 1.9989) at half the SDPA probe overhead; Lower-Half (0,1,2) scores 1.9832 +- 0.0010 and Long-Window (3,5) scores 1.9795 +- 0.0007. (b) Same-Trainer Matched-Time Comparisons (~21.6s fwd+rule): Inside the same exp49-51 trainer, 1,004-step 4-matrix WM (21.55s, 1.9720 +- 0.0006 DEV, 1.9392 +- 0.0004 VAL-B, 224.73 PPL) beats 720-step Full 6-Matrix M=2 (21.67s, 1.9763 +- 0.0009), whereas 840-step Upper-Half (3,4,5) M=2 (21.71s) reaches 1.9609 +- 0.0006 DEV BPB (1.9264 +- 0.0007 VAL-B, 218.03 PPL), beating 1,004-step 4-matrix by -0.0111 DEV BPB (-0.0128 VAL-B, -6.70 PPL) at matched training-region time; at 400 steps (10.32s), Upper-Half (3,4,5) M=2 matches 438-step 4-matrix (2.0454 +- 0.0012 DEV, 2.0085 +- 0.0015 VAL-B vs. 2.0096). (c) 720-Step M=4 + ve_gate & Exact-BP Controls: 720-step 6-matrix M=4 + ve_gate reaches 1.9683 +- 0.0007 DEV BPB (1.9334 +- 0.0008 VAL-B, 222.45 PPL in 28.57s), recovering 59.0% (-0.0306 of -0.0519 BPB) of the 720-step 4-to-6-matrix Exact-BP gain (1.9423 +- 0.0031 -> 1.8904 +- 0.0012). 2. Applied all v6 review notes: (a) corrected d6 parameter accounting (3 ve_gate matrices at blocks 1,3,5 = 576 weights + 12 scalars = 588 frozen entries; 26,345,472 = 99.9978% active); (b) defined Run GPU (fwd+rule) and separated exp37/39 (~18.8 ms/st) vs. exp49-51 (~21.6 ms/st) trainer curves in Fig. 1E; (c) framed ve_gate (-0.00047 +- 0.00064 BPB) as exploratory and specified Prop. 5's pre-rotary coordinate basis; (d) added explicit scope qualifications to the abstract.",
